9,"Tangale is a West Chadic language with about 200,000 speakers in...",https://www.omniglot.com/writing/tangale.htm,"Tangale is a member of the West Chadic branch of the Afro-Asiatic language family. It is spoken in eastern Nigeriais, mainly in Akko, Billiri, Kaltungo and Shongom Local Government Area of Gomba State, and also in Bauchi State. In 2006 there were about 200,000 of Tangale.",Tangale,Afro-Asiatic
